  "responsibleAiStatement": "Managely is designed to coach communication rather than make employment decisions. It never recommends firing, promoting, disciplining, or making legal, medical, or psychological judgments about any real person.",
  "privacyNotice": "Managely is a practice environment. Avoid entering names, medical information, private family information, or other sensitive information about real employees.",

  "privacyTitle": "Privacy & Responsible AI",
  "privacySection1Title": "Use fictional scenarios whenever possible",
  "privacySection1Body": "Managely works best with fictional or composite situations. You don't need real names, real details, or real outcomes to get useful practice.",
  "privacySection2Title": "Avoid personal information",
  "privacySection2Body": "Avoid entering real employees' names, medical information, family details, or anything you wouldn't want stored or reviewed.",
  "privacySection3Title": "AI feedback is coaching, not HR advice",
  "privacySection3Body": "Evaluations describe your communication patterns in this conversation only. They are not professional, legal, medical, or HR guidance.",
  "privacySection4Title": "Managely does not make employment decisions",
  "privacySection4Body": "Managely will never recommend firing, disciplining, promoting, or making salary or legal decisions about any real person. Those decisions belong to you, your manager, and your HR team.",

  "privacyPolicyHeading": "Privacy Policy",
  "privacyPolicyIntro": "This section explains what information Managely collects, how we use and share it, and the rights you have over it — including the rights given to users in Türkiye under the Personal Data Protection Law No. 6698 (KVKK).",
  "privacyDataCollectedTitle": "Information we collect",
  "privacyDataCollectedBody": "Account info (your name, email address, and profile photo); the scenarios you practice, your conversation transcripts, skill scores, and feedback; your optional real-conversation debrief notes; your subscription status and purchase events from the App Store or Google Play (Managely never sees your payment details — Apple and Google handle that); and basic device and usage data.",
  "privacyDataUseTitle": "How we use your information",
  "privacyDataUseBody": "To run the app's core features — generating the AI employee's replies, scoring your practice conversations, and tracking your progress; to verify your email and send account-related emails; to manage your subscription; and to keep the app reliable and safe. We never sell your data, and we never use it for third-party advertising.",
  "privacyDataShareTitle": "Who we share information with",
  "privacyDataShareBody": "Firebase (Google) for sign-in and data storage; Anthropic to generate the AI employee's replies and feedback; Apple App Store / Google Play to verify your purchases directly — Managely uses no third-party subscription vendor; Mailtrap to deliver account verification emails; and Google Cloud / Microsoft Azure to convert the AI employee's own replies to speech in Voice Mode. We don't share your data with anyone else, except where required by law.",
  "privacyRightsTitle": "Your rights, and how to delete your data",
  "privacyRightsBody": "You can update your profile from within the app at any time. For anything else — a copy of your data, or deleting your account entirely — email info@frontdreams.com from the address on your account. You have the right to: know whether we process your data and request a copy of it; know who we've shared it with; have inaccurate data corrected; have your data deleted once there's no reason left to keep it; have any correction or deletion passed on to the third parties above; object to a decision made about you based solely on automated processing; and claim compensation if you're harmed by unlawful processing. We respond within 30 days. Once a deletion request is confirmed, we permanently delete your account, practice transcripts, debrief notes, and subscription records, aside from anything we're legally required to keep briefly, such as billing records.",
  "privacyKvkkTitle": "Your rights under Turkish law (KVKK)",
  "privacyKvkkBody": "If you're in Türkiye, the rights above are the rights given to you as a veri sahibi (data subject) under Article 11 of the Personal Data Protection Law No. 6698 (KVKK). Front Dreams, as the operator of Managely, is the data controller (veri sorumlusu) for this data. Submit a KVKK request the same way as any other privacy request — email info@frontdreams.com from your account's address so we can verify it's you.",
  "privacyChildrenTitle": "Children's privacy",
  "privacyChildrenBody": "Managely is intended for working adults and is not directed at children under 16. We don't knowingly collect information from children.",
  "privacyContactTitle": "Contact us",
  "privacyContactBody": "Questions about this policy, your data, or a KVKK request? Email info@frontdreams.com.",

  "aboutTitle": "About Managely",
  "aboutTagline": "Practice before the stakes are real.",
  "aboutWhatManagelyDoesTitle": "What Managely Does",
  "aboutWhatManagelyDoesBody": "Managely is a practice space for the conversations new managers dread most — difficult feedback, saying no, setting boundaries, handling conflict. You roleplay with an AI \"employee\" that responds the way a real person would, then get a clear read on how you communicated. Nothing here evaluates or makes decisions about real employees — only your side of the conversation.",
  "aboutHowScoringWorksTitle": "How Scoring Works",
  "aboutHowScoringWorksBody": "Your starting scores come from a short situational-judgment assessment — realistic workplace scenarios with answer choices that vary in quality, not a self-rating you fill in yourself (self-ratings are notoriously unreliable; people tend to overrate themselves). From there, every practice conversation nudges your scores based on the same signals: specificity, tone, whether you listened before responding, and how you handled pushback.",
  "aboutScoresDisclaimer": "These scores are research-informed, not a certified clinical or psychometric instrument (like a licensed EQ-i or TKI assessment). Treat them as a useful signal for practice, not a formal evaluation.",
  "aboutSixSkillsTitle": "The Six Skills We Measure",
  "aboutSixSkillsSubtitle": "Each is drawn from a different, well-established framework used in real leadership and coaching training.",
  "aboutResponsibleAiTitle": "Responsible AI",
  "aboutVersionLine": "Managely · Version {version} ({buildNumber})",
  "@aboutVersionLine": {
    "placeholders": { "version": {"type": "String"}, "buildNumber": {"type": "String"} }
  },
  "aboutFrameworkEmpathyDescription": "Recognizing and responding to what someone else is feeling before reacting to what they said.",
  "aboutFrameworkEmpathyFramework": "Grounded in Goleman's Emotional Intelligence framework.",
  "aboutFrameworkClarityDescription": "Stating a specific, observable expectation instead of a vague impression.",
  "aboutFrameworkClarityFramework": "Grounded in the Center for Creative Leadership's SBI model (Situation-Behavior-Impact).",
  "aboutFrameworkAssertivenessDescription": "Saying what you need clearly and directly, without either backing down or steamrolling.",
  "aboutFrameworkAssertivenessFramework": "Grounded in DESC scripting (Bower & Bower assertiveness training).",
  "aboutFrameworkActiveListeningDescription": "Actually hearing someone out — reflecting back what they said before responding.",
  "aboutFrameworkActiveListeningFramework": "Grounded in Motivational Interviewing's OARS model (Open questions, Affirmations, Reflective listening, Summarizing).",
  "aboutFrameworkConflictDescription": "Handling disagreement in a way that resolves it, rather than avoiding or escalating it.",
  "aboutFrameworkConflictFramework": "Grounded in the Thomas-Kilmann Conflict Mode Instrument (TKI).",
  "aboutFrameworkBoundaryDescription": "Holding a fair line — for yourself or your team — without being harsh about it.",
  "aboutFrameworkBoundaryFramework": "Grounded in the Crucial Conversations framework (Patterson, Grenny, McMillan, Switzler).",

